  ],
  "version": "enrolled",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) TCA 2-7-112(c)(2), Section 1\n(quote) A valid identification card issued by the state of Tennessee, or the United States where authorized by law to issue personal identification; provided, that such identification card contains a photograph of the voter;\n(section) TCA 2-7-112(c)(5), Section 2\n(quote) A valid employee identification card issued by the state of Tennessee or the United States where authorized by law to issue employee identification; provided, that such identification card contains a photograph of the voter;\n(section) TCA 2-7-112(g), new, Section 3\n(quote) An identification card issued by a county or municipality or entity thereof, including a public library, containing a photograph shall not be evidence of identification for purposes of verifying the person's identification on the application for ballot.\n(b_no_id_remedy) not stated.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.\n(other) Sec 4: effective on becoming law.\n(other) version: Draft (only version saved): limits accepted photo IDs to State of Tennessee or United States issuers and bars county, city and library IDs (slot a). Senate amendments 1, 2, 3 and House amendments HA0155, HA0156, HA0195 are not saved, and neither is the enrolled or chaptered text, so what was enacted cannot be compared with this Draft.\n(other) note: Enacted as Public Chapter 178 after two House amendments (HA0155, HA0156) that the Senate concurred in; their content is unknown. House passed it by substituting it for companion HB229. Amendment 1 (Kyle) was tabled, Amendment 2 (Campfield) failed 10-20, Amendment 3 (Kyle, Rule 39(3)) failed 5-24 in the Senate; none is saved.",
